  "body": "Looking at the \"Introduction to Writable Streams\" example,\n\n``` js\nfunction makeWritableFileStream(filename, { highWaterMark = 16 * 1024 } = {}) {\n  const fileHandle = createRawFileHandle(filename, \"w\");\n\n  return new WritableStream({\n    write(data, done, error) {\n      fileHandle.write(data, writeErr => {\n        if (writeErr) {\n          fileHandle.close(closeErr => {\n            if (closeErr) {\n              error(closeErr);\n            }\n\n            error(writeErr);\n          });\n        } else {\n          done();\n        }\n      });\n    }\n}\n```\n\nCould `write` return a Promise instead of accepting `done` and `error` callbacks?\n\n``` js\nfunction makeWritableFileStream(filename, { highWaterMark = 16 * 1024 } = {}) {\n  const fileHandle = createRawFileHandle(filename, \"w\");\n\n  return new WritableStream({\n    write(data) {\n      return new Promise(function(done, error) {\n        fileHandle.write(data, writeErr => {\n          if (writeErr) {\n            fileHandle.close(closeErr => {\n              if (closeErr) {\n                error(closeErr);\n              }\n\n              error(writeErr);\n            });\n          } else {\n            done();\n          }\n        });\n      });\n    }\n}\n```\n\n/cc @domenic \n\n_(Apologies if you've already answered this in another issue already. Did a quick search and didn't find anything)_ \n",
